text-sm text-gray-700">Include x-default entry pointing to your default language version</p></div><div class="flex items-start gap-3"><div class="w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-[#00AEEF] text-white flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm font-bold">4</div><p class="text-sm text-gray-700">Copy generated tags and add them to the <!-- -->&lt;head&gt;<!-- --> section of ALL language versions</p></div></div></div><div class="bg-gradient-to-br from-gray-50 to-white border border-gray-200 rounded-lg p-6 md:p-8"><div class="mb-6"><div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-3"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-circle-question-mark w-5 h-5 text-[#00AEEF]" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle><path d="M9.09 9a3 3 0 0 1 5.83 1c0 2-3 3-3 3"></path><path d="M12 17h.01"></path></svg><h3 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-black">Frequently Asked Questions</h3></div><p class="text-sm md:text-base text-gray-600">Common questions about this tool and how to use it effectively</p></div><div class="bg-white rounded-lg border border-gray-200 p-4 md:p-6"><div class="border-b border-gray-200 last:border-0" ><button class="w-full py-6 flex items-start gap-4 text-left hover:bg-gray-50 -mx-4 px-4 rounded-lg transition-colors duration-200"><div class="flex-shrink-0 w-8 h-8 bg-[#00AEEF]/10 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center"><span class="text-sm font-bold text-[#00AEEF]">1</span></div><div class="flex-1 min-w-0"><h3 class="text-base md:text-lg font-semibold text-black">What are hreflang tags and why do I need them?</h3></div><div class="flex-shrink-0"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down w-5 h-5 text-gray-400" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></div></button><div class="faq-answer hidden px-4 pb-6 text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed" style="padding-left:3.5rem"><p>Hreflang tags tell search engines which language and regional version of a page to show users based on their location and language preferences. They're essential for multilingual or multi-regional websites to prevent duplicate content issues and ensure users see the correct version of your content in search results.</p></div></div><div class="border-b border-gray-200 last:border-0" ><button class="w-full py-6 flex items-start gap-4 text-left hover:bg-gray-50 -mx-4 px-4 rounded-lg transition-colors duration-200"><div class="flex-shrink-0 w-8 h-8 bg-[#00AEEF]/10 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center"><span class="text-sm font-bold text-[#00AEEF]">2</span></div><div class="flex-1 min-w-0"><h3 class="text-base md:text-lg font-semibold text-black">What&#x27;s the difference between language codes (en) and regional codes (en-US)?</h3></div><div class="flex-shrink-0"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down w-5 h-5 text-gray-400" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></div></button><div class="faq-answer hidden px-4 pb-6 text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed" style="padding-left:3.5rem"><p>Language-only codes (en, es, fr) target all speakers of that language regardless of location. Regional codes (en-US, en-GB) target specific country variations of a language. Use regional codes when content differs by country (pricing, terminology, availability). Use language-only codes for generic translations.</p></div></div><div class="border-b border-gray-200 last:border-0" ><button class="w-full py-6 flex items-start gap-4 text-left hover:bg-gray-50 -mx-4 px-4 rounded-lg transition-colors duration-200"><div class="flex-shrink-0 w-8 h-8 bg-[#00AEEF]/10 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center"><span class="text-sm font-bold text-[#00AEEF]">3</span></div><div class="flex-1 min-w-0"><h3 class="text-base md:text-lg font-semibold text-black">What is x-default and when should I use it?</h3></div><div class="flex-shrink-0"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down w-5 h-5 text-gray-400" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></div></button><div class="faq-answer hidden px-4 pb-6 text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed" style="padding-left:3.5rem"><p>x-default is a fallback URL that Google shows to users whose language preferences don't match any of your hreflang variations. It's best practice to always include x-default, typically pointing to your primary language version or a language selector page.</p></div></div><div class="border-b border-gray-200 last:border-0" ><button class="w-full py-6 flex items-start gap-4 text-left hover:bg-gray-50 -mx-4 px-4 rounded-lg transition-colors duration-200"><div class="flex-shrink-0 w-8 h-8 bg-[#00AEEF]/10 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center"><span class="text-sm font-bold text-[#00AEEF]">4</span></div><div class="flex-1 min-w-0"><h3 class="text-base md:text-lg font-semibold text-black">Should I use HTML tags or HTTP headers for hreflang?</h3></div><div class="flex-shrink-0"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down w-5 h-5 text-gray-400" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></div></button><div class="faq-answer hidden px-4 pb-6 text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed" style="padding-left:3.5rem"><p>HTML tags (in the <head> section) are the most common and easiest to implement. HTTP headers are useful for non-HTML files like PDFs. Both methods are equally valid from an SEO perspective, but don't use both simultaneously for the same page.</p></div></div><div class="border-b border-gray-200 last:border-0" ><button class="w-full py-6 flex items-start gap-4 text-left hover:bg-gray-50 -mx-4 px-4 rounded-lg transition-colors duration-200"><div class="flex-shrink-0 w-8 h-8 bg-[#00AEEF]/10 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center"><span class="text-sm font-bold text-[#00AEEF]">5</span></div><div class="flex-1 min-w-0"><h3 class="text-base md:text-lg font-semibold text-black">Do I need to add hreflang tags to every language version?</h3></div><div class="flex-shrink-0"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down w-5 h-5 text-gray-400" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></div></button><div class="faq-answer hidden px-4 pb-6 text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed" style="padding-left:3.5rem"><p>Yes! Each language version must include the complete set of hreflang tags pointing to all other versions AND itself. This is called bidirectional linking. If page A references page B, then page B must also reference page A.</p></div></div><div class="border-b border-gray-200 last:border-0" ><button class="w-full py-6 flex items-start gap-4 text-left hover:bg-gray-50 -mx-4 px-4 rounded-lg transition-colors duration-200"><div class="flex-shrink-0 w-8 h-8 bg-[#00AEEF]/10 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center"><span class="text-sm font-bold text-[#00AEEF]">6</span></div><div class="flex-1 min-w-0"><h3 class="text-base md:text-lg font-semibold text-black">How do I verify my hreflang implementation is correct?</h3></div><div class="flex-shrink-0"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down w-5 h-5 text-gray-400" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></div></button><div class="faq-answer hidden px-4 pb-6 text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed" style="padding-left:3.5rem"><p>Use Google Search Console's International Targeting report to check for hreflang errors. Common issues include missing return links, incorrect language codes, or wrong URLs. The report shows specific errors and which pages are affected.</p></div></div><div class="border-b border-gray-200 last:border-0" ><button class="w-full py-6 flex items-start gap-4 text-left hover:bg-gray-50 -mx-4 px-4 rounded-lg transition-colors duration-200"><div class="flex-shrink-0 w-8 h-8 bg-[#00AEEF]/10 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center"><span class="text-sm font-bold text-[#00AEEF]">7</span></div><div class="flex-1 min-w-0"><h3 class="text-base md:text-lg font-semibold text-black">What are the most common hreflang mistakes to avoid?</h3></div><div class="flex-shrink-0"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down w-5 h-5 text-gray-400" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></div></button><div class="faq-answer hidden px-4 pb-6 text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed" style="padding-left:3.5rem"><p>Common mistakes include: using relative URLs instead of absolute URLs, missing self-referential links (page not referencing itself), incorrect language codes, not including x-default, missing bidirectional links, and mixing HTML tags with HTTP headers. Our generator validates these issues automatically.</p></div></div></div><div class="mt-6 text-center" ><p class="text-sm text-gray-600 mb-2">Still have questions?</p><a href="/contact" class="text-[#00AEEF] font-semibold hover:und